      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This bug also applies to GNU/Linux, which is especially sad because Unity 2019 is the fist Unity version with full GNU/Linux support.\nBecause the problem is within one of the VRCSDK dlls it's hard to manually fix it. The check for the VRC client installation shouldn't be done before \"Build and Publish\" because it's not required. I assume on Windows it will build fine if it doesn't detect the VRC folder and just write a warning in the log. The error could just be turned into a warning and not stop the complete process.\nI know that official VRC client support of Linux is basically impossible but it runs very well with proton so a Windows installation isn't really required for playing VRC. With the Quest version that's even more the case. Running the Unity Editor in proton would be annoying because it perfectly works natively.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
